From: mklab <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 35/35] record arch/amd64/boot.h, which the port needed and the record did not have

arch/amd64/boot.c has `#include "boot.h"` and arch/amd64 had no such header --
arch/x86 gained one in an upstream sweep that never reached this directory,
because nothing compiled it. Spike 1 wrote the file; nothing ever recorded it.

It surfaced on 2026-08-27 from the completeness check that binds the numbered
record to patches/TESTED-TREE.patch: 49 of the 50 files in the built divergence
were named by some numbered patch, and this was the one that was not. The port
had been compiling against a file no patch mentioned.

Arch-tested: amd64 (cold build from a pristine pin, 2026-08-27)

diff --git a/arch/amd64/boot.h b/arch/amd64/boot.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..84136f1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/amd64/boot.h
@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+/* tag: openbios loader prototypes for amd64
+ *
+ * Spike 1: arch/x86 has had this header since the sweep that introduced it;
+ * arch/amd64 never gained one because nothing compiled this directory.
+ *
+ * See the file "COPYING" for further information about
+ * the copyright and warranty status of this work.
+ */
+
+/* linux_load.c */
+int linux_load(struct sys_info *info, const char *file, const char *cmdline);
+
+/* boot.c */
+extern void boot(void);
